<article class=3D"article-container">
  <h1>OACOK, OKOCA, or OCOKA?</h1>
  <h2>Reframing Terrain Analysis for Cyberspace</h2>
  <p class=3D"lead">By Maj. JC Fernandes and Maj. Alexander Master</p>
  <p>
    <strong>Article published on:</strong> July 1st, 2025 in the Gray Space=
 Summer 2025 Edition
  </p>
  <p>
    <span class=3D"label label-asw">Read Time:</span> <span class=3D"articl=
e-time">&lt; 8 mins</span>
  </p>

  <figure class=3D"image-container">
    <img alt=3D"Military tactical map showing terrain analysis with Governm=
ent Complex and Military Complex marked. Purple K symbols indicate key terr=
ain positions. Map legend shows symbols for avenues of approach, airfield, =
battalion mobility corridors, bridges, buildings, ferry routes, harbor, int=
ernational border, minefields, restricted terrain types, roads, and urban a=
reas. Green crosshatched areas represent severely restricted terrain, black=
 crosshatched areas show urban terrain." src=3D"https://www.lineofdeparture=
.army.mil/portals/144/Images/Journals/Gray-Space/Gray-Space-First-Edition-2=
025/Terrain-Analysis-img1.jpg">
    <figcaption class=3D"cutline">
      Figure 1: Modified combined obstacle overlay highlighting the key asp=
ects of terrain analysis.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <audio class=3D"scrolled-into-view" controls=3D"" preload=3D"none" aria-l=
abel=3D"Audio narration of article" id=3D"audioPlayer">
    <source src=3D"https://www.lineofdeparture.army.mil/portals/144/MP3/Gra=
